    "attributes": {
        "action": "Mandate That Adverts Disclose Use Of Animal Testing",
        "additional_details": "A 2026 YouGov poll conducted by Naturewatch Foundation shows 74% of UK adults are unclear about what \"cruelty-free\" means. People want transparency. Consumers have the right to that information.",
        "background": "We ask that the Government make all advertisements clearly disclose whether products have been tested on animals, so consumers can make informed decisions, in line with the principles behind section 227 of the Digital Markets, Competition and Consumers Act 2024.",
